<%#
  The reCAPTCHA script, loaded without competing with the page.

  Expects `captcha` = { siteKey, version }. Emits nothing without a site key, so
  a site that has the toggles on but no keys never pulls Google's script.

  The two versions need different URLs and neither works with the other's key:

    v3       - the site key goes IN the URL, and Google starts scoring
               immediately on load.
    v2       - `render=explicit` tells Google not to touch the markup, so
               main.js can render each widget itself and hold the widget ids.
               With auto-render, `grecaptcha.execute()` falls back to "the first
               widget on the page", which is wrong the moment a page has two.

  Kept in one file because the six templates that need it were each carrying
  their own copy, and they had already drifted apart once.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Why the src is deferred

  `async defer` stops the script blocking the parser, but it does not stop the
  download competing with everything else. It is a third-party bundle - around
  340 KB, plus a 35 KB stylesheet, plus two more connections to gstatic.com -
  and it was fetched on page load on every page that carries a form. On a
  throttled mobile connection that is most of the bytes of the page, spent on a
  widget most visitors never reach, and it lands right in the window the first
  paint is trying to use.

  So the URL is parked in a data attribute and injected by main.js once the page
  is idle or the visitor touches anything. Anything that actually submits waits
  on `whenRecaptchaReady()`, which polls for `grecaptcha` - so a submit that
  beats the loader still works, it just waits for the script rather than sending
  an unverified form.

  The <noscript> copy keeps the old behaviour for JavaScript being off, where
  the loader would never run.
%>
<% if (captcha && captcha.siteKey) { %>
  <%
    var src = captcha.version === 'v3'
      ? 'https://www.google.com/recaptcha/api.js?render=' + encodeURIComponent(captcha.siteKey)
      : 'https://www.google.com/recaptcha/api.js?render=explicit';
  %>
  <span data-recaptcha-src="<%= src %>" hidden></span>
  <noscript>
    <script src="<%= src %>" async defer></script>
  </noscript>
<% } %>
